.eslintcache

# The worktree inventory, and only the one at the repository root.
#
# `scripts/worktree-inventory.mjs` writes a document about THIS machine: session
# ids, chat ids, absolute worktree paths, swarm claims and a `generatedAt`
# timestamp. None of it describes the repository, so tracking it bought churn —
# every agent that regenerated it produced a diff, and two agents regenerating it
# concurrently produced a merge conflict in a file that carries no reviewable
# meaning. A worktree's own copy lives under `.kilo/worktrees/` and is already
# covered by the `.kilo` line below.
#
# It is untracked, and a test enforces that: `worktree-inventory.test.mjs` fails
# if this file is tracked or if this rule is deleted. The generator, the curated
# table, and every finding are all still tracked — only the output is not.
/WORKTREES.json

.kilo
.serena

